# Docker build context exclusions for the root Dockerfile.
#
# Without this file the context is the entire repository, and `docker build .`
# ships it all to the daemon on every build.  The bulk is
# mini-agent-desktop/node_modules — thousands of files that no backend image
# ever references.

# Build output: recompiled inside the image, and the agent's target/ holds a
# ~500 MB fat jar that would be copied in only to be overwritten.
**/target/

# Desktop shell (Electron).  Not a Maven module and not copied by the
# Dockerfile — it is packaged by scripts/build-desktop.mjs instead.
mini-agent-desktop/

# Working artefacts and scratch directories.
*.log
.verify/
_pin_verify/
scripts/
docs/
skills/
_bak/
.git/
.gitignore
.workbuddy/

# Model weights, in case anything is ever built from the repository root.
#
# NOTE: this does NOT cover the embedding image.  Its build context is
# ./embedding-server, and Docker looks for a .dockerignore *inside* the context
# directory — it never falls back to this one.  So the weights below still get
# shipped to the daemon when `docker compose build` runs.
# Adding ./embedding-server/.dockerignore would cut that, but it changes what
# the embedding image can see and is therefore a separate, verifiable change.
embedding-server/models/
embedding-server/**/*.safetensors
